.TH KAGI-VOLUME-LIBVIRT-SCSI 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi \- print libvirt XML for a Kagi-backed SCSI disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi
.BR virtio-scsi | sas
.I HOST PORT
.RI [ TARGET ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints a SCSI controller and network disk fragment for a libvirt domain.
Use
.B virtio-scsi
for a paravirtualized controller or
.B sas
for the
.B lsisas1068
controller model.
The disk connects to the compatibility NBD export
.B keyspace
on the specified host and port.
.PP
The target device defaults to
.BR sda .
The disk sets
.B discard=unmap
so a supported guest's discard requests can reach Kagi's sparse volume.
Review the controller index and disk target before adding the fragment to an
existing domain.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-volume-nbd (1),
.BR kagi-volume-qemu-scsi (1),
.BR virsh (1)
